ZLUDA: post-phase kernels for native overrides. A native code object may define NAME_post1 .. NAME_post8; the hook
launches them after NAME on the same stream with the same parameters (u32 globals d4r_postK_grid_x/_grid_y, 0 = the
launch's grid; d4r_postK_block_x/_y/_z, 0 = 32/1/1). Preset K's bottleneck layer (dec5) runs as four phase kernels.

